        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "28334c3b-7add-5896-ac55-f8d64da280ba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Blake Debassige, Norval Morrisseau, Carmen Robertson\n- Places: West Bay, Manitoulin Island, Ontario\n- Organizations: M'Chigeeng First Nation\n- Topics: Aboriginal Canadian art, writings about Norval Morrisseau\n\nFacts:\n- Norval Morrisseau was born on March 14, 1932, and he was an Aboriginal Canadian artist also known as Copper Thunderbird.\n- Blake Debassige was born on June 22, 1956, at West Bay on Manitoulin Island in Ontario, and he is a Native Canadian artist of the M'Chigeeng First Nation.\n- Carmen Robertson wrote a number of works that focus on the Aboriginal Canadian artist Norval Morrisseau.\n- Norval Morrisseau died on December 4, 2007.",
